#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176826} :activity/id #uuid "8f647d7f-d10f-52b0-a5c4-c95324d956b1" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050269 :topic/id #uuid "3b1ff160-959d-503b-acf5-2be698a50baa" :topic/math-academy-id 3595} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176826 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186177047 :tutorial/content "Given a dataset of paired numerical observations $(x,y)$ and the corresponding linear regression model $\\widehat{y} =f(x),$ the **residual** for a particular observation $(x, y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-f(x) \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe subtract the *estimated* value predicted by the model from the actual *observed* value.\n\nTo illustrate this concept graphically, consider the following example.\n\nThe owner of an ice cream shop keeps track of the average daily temperature $x$ (measured in $^\\circ \\mathrm{F}$) and the resulting daily ice cream sales $y$ (in dollars). The scatter plot for several randomly selected days and the corresponding linear regression line are shown below. \n\n![](images/fc/fc149b8d911a7a9863df9cc25c635d6155accd676e83e335a65d9083596b779b.png)\n\nSuppose the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny= 2.5 x +165.\n$$\n\nLet's use our regression line to compute the residual of the point with coordinates $\\color{red}(82, 360)$ (shown in red on our graph). \n\nFirst, notice that since the highlighted data point has coordinates ${\\color{red}(82, 360)},$ our actual value is $y = {\\color{red}360}.$\n\nNext, we compute the predicted value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{y} & =2.5x+165 \\\\  & =2.5(82)+165 \\\\  & =370\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n![](images/38/3843c71b50251ae035378507ffb22cfade48dff8e1544d8e1317e4e6d611f7a1.png)\n\nFinally, we compute the residual: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =360-370 \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n     \n\nThe residual tells us that the linear model *overestimates* the true volume of ice cream sales by $\\[math]10$ when the outside temperature is $82^\\circ\\,\\textrm{F}.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "7e5cd2f9-494e-5533-98e9-c24f42631dad" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5968 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "56d03218-9fd1-5cb5-a471-09641e54c0ea" :step/math-academy-id 36423 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176828}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176827 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176033 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175888 :question/id #uuid "bc4500bc-8992-5148-95eb-6f84ae2508cf" :question/math-academy-id "e-9717"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e77a14c-9943-5494-ae89-a77c7a1888d0" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049868}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176341} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176342} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524960} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525051} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543550} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543562} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543587} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554595} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554645}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining Residuals From a Graph"} :step/id #uuid "d5ff3834-5f43-5149-a054-8bfcbb8b3bbf" :step/math-academy-id 36424 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176829}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176828 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176034 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175889 :question/id #uuid "cb2190d0-5150-53ff-b7ab-ed364611bc8f" :question/math-academy-id "e-9718"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0286d36b-217f-52e4-8580-e031b6dea31e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050210}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176339} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176340} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554579} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554610} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554631} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554642}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing Residuals Using the Regression Line Equation"} :step/id #uuid "2dbc11bb-69e2-5610-9c8e-28e53d57e103" :step/math-academy-id 36425 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176827}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176829 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186177048 :tutorial/content "A **residual plot** displays the values of the independent variable along the horizontal axis and the residuals along the vertical axis. \n\nThe scatter plot below represents data from a four-day sample on the number of people visiting a swimming pool and the average daytime temperature, in degrees Celsius. The line $\\ell$ is the corresponding linear regression line. \n\n![](images/62/6228578012fac7e42bedeb7ab7ad5fc9f42432aed8d5751b675df560bc867417.png)\n\n    \n\nThese residuals for each of the four data points are highlighted below:\n\n![](images/d7/d70c44fe7b8fce43a8962ac104651acced75e10598e865a3b3c80d09f16ce234.png)\n\n    \n\nIf we calculate the numerical values for the residuals at each data point (from left to right), we get the following results:\n\n$$\n-4, \\quad 8, \\quad -8, \\quad 4\n$$\n\nTo compute our residual plot, we plot each $x$-value and its corresponding residual on some coordinate axes: \n\n![](images/ff/ff8e6da5489313f1f981c379505f9a72610dfd2a4b5dc0113685d647ba02a1f3.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "ddf8fe09-fc0b-546d-942f-17a086708a11" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5969 :tutorial/title "Residual Plots"} :step/id #uuid "e65742ab-c850-50fd-b1a4-0670ddc16c2b" :step/math-academy-id 36426 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176833}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176830 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176035 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175890 :question/id #uuid "3b40900e-ca06-5951-8261-aa13d8f966ce" :question/math-academy-id "e-9719"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa97e57a-70d8-5708-8b7d-fa05604a3f88" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176343} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176344} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233432} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554547} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554549} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554634}] :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Residual Plots"} :step/id #uuid "a7847754-3ac7-5ffa-af5a-838c5d3e8886" :step/math-academy-id 36427} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176833 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186177051 :tutorial/content "![](images/ff/ff8e6da5489313f1f981c379505f9a72610dfd2a4b5dc0113685d647ba02a1f3.png)\n\nWe should be aware of the following interpretations for residual plots:\n\n- Any point *above* the horizontal axis represents a *positive* residual. A positive residual means that the regression model *underestimates* the observed value for $y$ at this point.\n\n- Any point *below* the horizontal axis represents a *negative* residual. A negative residual means that the regression model *overestimates* the observed value for $y$ at this point.\n\nResidual plots can also be used to assess whether a trend line is a \"good\" fit for the corresponding data:\n\n- If a linear trend line is a good fit for the data, the residuals should be scattered randomly above and below the horizontal axis and be relatively close to zero.\n\n- In cases where the residuals show some clear pattern, this usually indicates that the data has no linear trend.\n\nThe residuals are scattered randomly about the horizontal axis in our last example. However, they are not close to zero, indicating that the trend line is a weak fit for the data." :tutorial/id #uuid "d7794124-93e8-5abb-8a78-4c8884a07547" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6034 :tutorial/title "Properties of Residual Plots"} :step/id #uuid "3fdb60d4-7e70-551a-9e4a-8bb61625c9cc" :step/math-academy-id 36805 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176830}}] :activity/title "Residuals and Residual Plots" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186176138}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525099} :activity/id #uuid "1565ea4e-c392-50d1-9414-12d443b010cf" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050269 :topic/id #uuid "3b1ff160-959d-503b-acf5-2be698a50baa" :topic/math-academy-id 3595} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525092 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524960 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "155561b0-11da-52be-a290-8bc7fd41e681" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524422} {:answer/id #uuid "56a2ddd1-cadc-5a93-9a25-8dddff01f271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524532} {:answer/id #uuid "aefdfe8c-fa67-577b-98ee-259e0b602d66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524663} {:answer/id #uuid "e0fe8d85-7874-5929-8753-4945ee9ab9ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524773} {:answer/id #uuid "e2a545ba-ef49-5db8-a0d9-0458f6933545" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524778}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524773} :answer-field/id #uuid "48948107-5211-5ac2-9e2d-522c9771683b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "06429645-5834-5aa5-be8c-7530ab34a0e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-134787" :question/problem "![](images/55/553af60aa28cbdd7565259eacc167187bc9c63a5b30cd78a6c14a3c43603fca2.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(5,3).$ So, our actual value is $y=3.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=5$ has the $y$-coordinate $5.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=5.$\n\n![](images/c5/c558c80b7056b794534146d3b99f399c3084806758f78bd6eddb39e8c89248e9.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =3-5 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4f48dbfb-61be-5cd7-8c7c-7f3723f848b5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525098}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525098 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525051 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "288479be-98bd-57e4-9608-f6f04980af8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524457} {:answer/id #uuid "a92e5308-f602-5b56-8117-08f3a63517ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524653} {:answer/id #uuid "cc7640de-088c-554a-a442-df97fc11d882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524720} {:answer/id #uuid "e5da0595-ab74-5f54-bd61-a8b4f9a3237a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524785} {:answer/id #uuid "ffffc3bb-9a0e-59c2-9d08-ba493528be35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524841}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524457} :answer-field/id #uuid "c15ed523-3e32-50d6-b2d3-15996b2f731b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524922}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e01898f3-3b5c-52d9-b3b4-b90e7c403824" :question/math-academy-id "q-134799" :question/problem "![](images/ae/ae35183698308f87acb254b7141d025bc55f815c49dea54231c713997c6a22eb.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(10,4).$ So, our actual value is $y=4.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=10$ has the $y$-coordinate $8.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=8.$\n\n![](images/61/61ed1ba4b285ac0d21410ddde91c3ed3882def52cbc500867aa7184114dd8fd8.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =4-8 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "5cc55bd4-2c1a-5ba9-bb47-99a6d6d6d26a"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525099 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176341 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf731189-32fe-57a4-bde5-3c54274327ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174305} {:answer/id #uuid "1a6379b8-ece0-5a99-844b-b7f486334f38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174306} {:answer/id #uuid "441aa6e9-1299-567b-858c-691df1df7a1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174307} {:answer/id #uuid "4b4cb6ac-32c3-5dd7-9a8f-634d8cdf9d9d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174308} {:answer/id #uuid "621b8204-3932-59dd-b595-a75ccb8e4c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174309}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186174308} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5802a2f-64ed-5fd4-b9cc-65c0cef24d68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dd98bac0-93e8-506d-a8ba-d1595548f912" :question/math-academy-id "q-134267" :question/problem "![](images/a7/a7fb89105bc5a11837ed0f416b2327d88202e8e782fa4c114ac47b3d5d15421c.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(7,-2).$ So, our actual value is $y=-2.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=7$ has the $y$-coordinate $-4.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=-4.$\n\n![](images/92/92a26b8ab019879dec3208878f6a0604c0616776b09e3f8fa916fcab72df3a73.png)\n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =-2-(-4) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "674c6b2d-1d05-59d6-90ed-5b152a4fab06" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525092}}] :activity/title "Residuals and Residual Plots" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186524363}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543601} :activity/id #uuid "ef56f8ca-db40-565e-bd1c-7c7a8fb3e9b0" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050269 :topic/id #uuid "3b1ff160-959d-503b-acf5-2be698a50baa" :topic/math-academy-id 3595} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543601 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543562 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00765988-b24e-516e-81a5-803465b2cbab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542636} {:answer/id #uuid "2fb61cf0-8148-5e19-85df-5a17cfbc10f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542766} {:answer/id #uuid "6dfd5478-a857-5295-91e8-3b663a1bc7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542933} {:answer/id #uuid "ba0a7473-8f7d-5f9a-97c9-726d94e6f4b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543126} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b10261-e8cd-557e-a60d-49043c55ee7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543256}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543126} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8c336d7-1f88-5669-a3cc-3ac8dd456feb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d6509173-6968-54cb-999d-d5fe096ebbff" :question/math-academy-id "q-134798" :question/problem "![](images/b3/b375c1e162a9f1c2892903c20606921673498579f9b41f633447832fd3ea2192.png)\n\nThe scatter plot for the data sets $x$ and $y$ of paired observations and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(4,70).$ So, our actual value is $y=70.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=4$ has the $y$-coordinate $50.$ So, our estimated value of is $\\overset{^}{y}=50.$\n\n![](images/04/041f64255345edf7ac37bd61e0ab97a93cc2696f028a53ba0896e0659966c2d8.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the residual is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =70-50 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "106ec1c5-5aeb-55e4-9a89-04cf9274a237" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543618}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543618 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543587 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b317e2f-e6dd-53e0-9e49-ee9c188855d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-0.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542753} {:answer/id #uuid "49bc7362-977c-5232-be6c-b5cfdd1ef847" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542844} {:answer/id #uuid "5619b467-5b18-5824-9a47-f5bbd8a4a4a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542873} {:answer/id #uuid "612936c1-41a2-55be-bcc4-3b8cf0813d4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.5\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542902} {:answer/id #uuid "b26c54e1-c250-50fe-b5f2-37358d367201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543105}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542873} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f4f4e5c-e51e-5cea-9a0b-324f1c69bce1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f1b17b2b-5f71-5d88-80f9-025ec7f6d205" :question/math-academy-id "q-134808" :question/problem "![](images/08/08ce939458d5c298805692df7d10bed2abdcf81ec874da3f61dbe15f59fc141a.png)\n\nA biologist records the heights $y$ (in meters) of several oak trees at certain times $x$ (in years) after they were planted. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.  \n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(6,6.5).$ So, our actual value is $y=6.5.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=6$ has the $y$-coordinate $5.5.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=5.5.$\n\n![](images/ee/eedd1cadb2ba49fb95f9e18f9bef365942e53521e6894a270c9a1e1474f3ed71.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =6.5-5.5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $1\\,\\text{m}.$"} :step/id #uuid "328f4cd9-6f09-53f8-b7dd-274af5b0a028" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543628}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543628 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543550 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "111c354b-41eb-5072-82a1-a27b376ef779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542679} {:answer/id #uuid "32b8dd5f-70e9-5121-9de5-389361fe1956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-25\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542777} {:answer/id #uuid "3eb6331c-9c5e-5112-8172-2d2c6ae715e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "20\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542810} {:answer/id #uuid "5ecc3dc4-f5bd-51df-a791-7eef362a46eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "50\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542895} {:answer/id #uuid "6748c281-3aeb-5426-9750-d7329ae49821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-15\\,kg" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542918}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542777} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ed40114-2ba1-5996-b505-11a621544fa9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b2848e9c-e485-5752-8daf-a5d57b496ccb" :question/math-academy-id "q-134812" :question/problem "![](images/24/243a4212d1128a79203493bf672ad1c956fe0f48aad6abbb910de2861d99669c.png)\n\nA dog food company records data on the number of dogs $(x)$ sheltered at some kennels across the country and the corresponding amount of dog food $y$ (in kilograms) consumed in a month. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above. \n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted data point?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(10,175).$ So, our actual value is $y=175.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=10$ has the $y$-coordinate $200.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=200.$\n\n![](images/2c/2cd59a9ae9c7ad474a9d5a308d4b8f3c9b96be70acdf1e3613dfc4757ff01766.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =175-200 \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $-25\\,kg.$"} :step/id #uuid "47edabd6-568a-5a2a-87d9-33d6db405e8a"}] :activity/title "Residuals and Residual Plots" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542632}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571519} :activity/id #uuid "6e4c5edf-99ca-525c-a6e8-fa582f571ea0" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050269 :topic/id #uuid "3b1ff160-959d-503b-acf5-2be698a50baa" :topic/math-academy-id 3595} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571469 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554645 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d738011-9f4c-5d4e-a309-ef64a768c823" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$1\\,200$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554051} {:answer/id #uuid "a9b7e43c-40c5-5e6a-932e-71b4efd2aa35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$1\\,000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554247} {:answer/id #uuid "d48ea0cd-c010-5dea-b3a7-cfb311eab498" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$2\\,000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554330} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b52400-e104-580d-9769-33accdba452b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$1\\,500$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554362} {:answer/id #uuid "eb398d66-b3c7-5535-b999-ccfa4a862a14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$2\\,500$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554382}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554330} :answer-field/id #uuid "2802197e-59f8-5a42-85de-d389505bc4f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fd84baa2-dbd3-5523-aca7-04ab311e0400" :question/math-academy-id "q-134797" :question/problem "![](images/81/815ba0a13bc8cbd7adcfadc63b80d6f2da36c9755166694915fa2f297be27721.png)\n\nAn employee of a car dealership collects data on the value $y$ (in thousands of dollars) of a particular car model $x$ years after its release to the market. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe highlighted datapoint has coordinates $(6,12).$ So, our actual value is $y=12.$\n\nOn the other hand, the point on the regression line that corresponds to $x=6$ has the $y$-coordinate $10.$ So, our estimated value is $\\overset{^}{y}=10.$\n\n![](images/ab/ab5e194ac03482b1cee6bdb7aa35e323b40a1ad63769e60acbb000adb7aa1e82.png)\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\overset{^}{y} \\\\  & =12-10 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $$2\\,000.$"} :step/id #uuid "2c0eb85e-9eec-5f4f-b6fc-97a5c56860cb"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571487 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176344 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "876ae649-11c0-5089-87dc-610f0036aa66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174323} {:answer/id #uuid "bc491ea0-1e09-56eb-9a79-d9be42023692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174324} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf618da-5927-578f-8feb-6bd70f6b8776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174325} {:answer/id #uuid "628ea2d3-dc5f-50b2-81c5-9a43908bb256" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174326} {:answer/id #uuid "6dda488a-d9e3-59a8-81f5-6f9dde1a3f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174327}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6d0d5456-fec0-5301-ba47-002165462cdb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7ae43775-06ac-519f-ac5d-57c73d122d92" :question/math-academy-id "q-134285" :question/problem "![](images/0e/0e3debd878c7c147ce9978bec054fc9d5c9a490bd094060ec1dd3c6ad56ecac9.png)\n\nAn antique broker has records about the value of an artwork $y$ (in thousands of dollars) at certain times $t$ (in decades) since the artwork was produced. The residual plot above was constructed after fitting a linear regression model on this data set. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n1. When $t = 5$, the regression equation underestimates the value of $y$.\n2. The residuals appear randomly scattered about the horizontal axis (there are no obvious trends).\n3. This linear regression is probably a good fit for the data."} :step/id #uuid "749adcf2-3609-57ef-a88a-58f98584fb0f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571469}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571519 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176342 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a774593d-dc82-5d50-8667-fb9ab35ab5db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$(-10000)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174311} {:answer/id #uuid "be631636-35f9-5288-8344-819217c75758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$5000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174312} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a353ec-507e-5e8c-a1d6-f5c33eae2784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$(-5000)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174313} {:answer/id #uuid "fac8b2f2-21e2-5ba4-9832-76e2f12eff72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$10000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174314} {:answer/id #uuid "7a22e90f-667d-50ab-9770-629412ff6774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174315}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6dc00c1c-9fd6-5d82-925a-2adc1e918fcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e312e8e0-12d2-524c-8d6c-c3bb62aee103" :question/math-academy-id "q-134276" :question/problem "![](images/15/15d2ded66d86366f481f5e88e3b45fbfc7e4d227b9f49aee35797554412fbb87.png)\n\nAn antique broker has records about the value of an artwork $y$ (in thousands of dollars) at certain times $t$ (in decades) since the artwork was produced. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?"} :step/id #uuid "fc3683d1-ce01-56ab-b8d9-ad456743c55e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186571487}}] :activity/title "Residuals and Residual Plots" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186570884}]}
